repository-code: 'https://github.com/unfoldtoolbox/UnfoldBIDS.jl'
abstract: >-
  The increasing complexity of naturalistic experiments
  requires advanced analytical methods, with the
  regression-based event-related potential (rERP) framework
  emerging as a promising tool for flexible, single-trial
  EEG analysis. Alongside methodological progress, the Brain
  Imaging Data Structure (BIDS) has revolutionized data
  sharing by standardizing file organization and enabling
  seamless integration across tools and pipelines. However,
  bridging these advancements, rERP modeling and
  BIDS-compliant datasets, typically requires cumbersome
  custom scripting, limiting reproducibility and efficiency.
    Here, we introduce UnfoldBIDS.jl, a Julia package that integrates BIDS-structured datasets with the rERP capabilities of Unfold.jl, streamlining the analysis of large-scale EEG datasets. The package simplifies analyses of BIDS-datasets, allows for preprocessing using MNE-python, returns tidy datasets for visualization or further statistical analysis and includes both documentation and tutorials.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - ERP
  - Unfold.jl
  - BIDS
  - Julia
